------------------------
Random Notes and musings
------------------------
Updating xOBSE to the newest version broke some scripts - do not do. GOG Nehrim has a reasonably recent version (xOBSE 22.7)
It is said that codecs packs should be removed - caused freezes every minute for someone
It is said that "Memory Purge" should be turned off, caused crashes when loading new areas
Oblivion should support 21:9 resolution, though with harmless glitches in loading screens (which are patched)
some people claim that proton9 works better for Oblivion.
MO2 did not seem to work well. Just using Wrye bash is suggested for Nehrim / Oblivion
BethINI did not seem to work well - It's settings caused some stuttering, and I seemed to crash entering cells with it on. Also overwrites a bunch of settings that the Nehrim launcher makes in the .ini. Not recommended
Don't want Lods - they just add extra load to the game.
